8\"><img src=\"https://link.axios.com/img/6a14a774a4e0095e0a03c94asknrd.99ka/e8cd8558.gif\" alt=\"\" border=\"0\" /></a></td>\r\n<td style=\"padding-right:3.5%\" align=\"right\"> <a href=\"https://link.axios.com/click/47993161.432298/aHR0cHM6Ly93d3cuYXhpb3MuY29tL25ld3NsZXR0ZXJzL2F4aW9zLWZpbmlzaC1saW5lLTQxNDFlNDk1LWMzZGEtNGJmOC05N2FjLWVlOTExNzRlOWEyOC5odG1sP3V0bV9zb3VyY2U9bmV3c2xldHRlciZ1dG1fbWVkaXVtPWVtYWlsJnV0bV9jYW1wYWlnbj1uZXdzbGV0dGVyX2F4aW9zZmluaXNobGluZSZzdHJlYW09dG9w/6a14a774a4e0095e0a03c94aBa125b095\" target=\"_blank\" class=\"b\" style=\"color:#222;font-size:13px;font-family:'gordita',Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif;text-decoration:underline\">View in browser</a> </td>\r\n</tr>\r\n</table>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr>\r\n<td height=\"30\" style=\"height:30px;font-size:0\">&nbsp;</td>\r\n</tr>  <tr>\r\n<td style=\"text-align:center;line-height:1.3\">  <span class=\"b\" style=\"font-size:11px;letter-spacing:1.4px;color:#222;font-family:'gorditamedium',Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif\">PRESENTED BY PEPSICO </span>  </td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr>\r\n<td height=\"16\" style=\"height:16px;font-size:0\">&nbsp;</td>\r\n</tr><tr>\r\n<td style=\"text-align:center;line-height:1\">\r\n<span class=\"s\" style=\"font-size:44px;font-family:'gorditamedium',Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif;color:#008dc8;letter-spacing:-1px;line-height:1\"> Axios Finish Line </span>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr>\r\n<td style=\"text-align:center;line-height:1.5;padding-bottom:35px;padding-top:10px\">\r\n<span class=\"b\" style=\"font-size:13px;color:#222;font-family:'gorditamedium',Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif\">By  Mike Allen and Erica Pandey and Jim VandeHei  <span style=\"margin:0 6px\">&middot;</span> Oct 19, 2026 </span>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr><tr>\r\n<td class=\"v\" style=\"font-size:17px;font-family:Georgia,serif;line-height:1.75;color:#222;letter-spacing:-0.1px;padding:0 3.5%\"><p><strong>Welcome back! </strong><em>Smart Brevity™ count: 391 words … 1½ mins. Edited by Natalie Daher and copy edited by Amy Stern.</em></p></td>\r\n</tr><tr>\r\n<td height=\"10\" style=\"height:10px;font-size:0;border-bottom:10px solid #f5f5f5\">&nbsp;</td>\r\n</tr>      <tr>\r\n<td height=\"10\" style=\"height:10px;font-size:0\">&nbsp;</td>\r\n</tr><tr>\r\n<td style=\"padding:20px 3.5% 10px;line-height:1.5\">\r\n<span class=\"b k\" style=\"font-size:27px;font-family:'gorditamedium',Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif;color:#222;letter-spacing:-0.1px;line-height:1.5\">  1 big thing: Your face needs a break </span>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>   <tr>\r\n<td height=\"10\" style=\"height:10px;font-size:0\">&nbsp;</td>\r\n</tr> <tr>\r\n<td class=\"v\" style=\"padding:0 3.5%;line-height:1.75;font-size:17px;font-family:Georgia,serif;color:#222;letter-spacing:-0.1px\"><div align=\"center\"><!--[if mso]><img alt='' src='https://images.axios.com/dW0TKn6-Zq0vKdxP6-T-Xfo9PrE=/fit-in/1116x1300/2026/10/19/1792426715469.jpeg' style='display:block; margin: 0 auto; max-width:100%;' width='558' /><![endif]--><!--[if !mso]><!--><img alt=\"\" src=\"https://images.axios.com/dW0TKn6-Zq0vKdxP6-T-Xfo9PrE=/fit-in/1116x1300/2026/10/19/1792426715469.jpeg\" style=\"display:block; margin: 0 auto; max-width:100%;\" width=\"100%\"/><!--<![endif]--></div> <div class=\"bodytext\" style=\"font-size:13px; font-family:'Gordita',Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif; color:#848484; margin-bottom:20px;\">An esthetician massages a client's face. Photo: Hyoung Chang/The Denver Post via Getty Images</div><p><strong>One spot </strong>getting more massage treatment: The face.</p><p><strong>The big picture: </strong>Facial massage is gaining popularity as people seek relief from tension and a new way to relax, <em>Axios' Carly Mallenbaum reports.</em></p><ul><li><strong>\"We're holding </strong>more tension in the face,\" thanks partly to the strain of looking at screens, Twin Cities esthetician Christina Snead tells Axios.</li><li><strong>Think</strong> forehead, jaw and chin.</li></ul><p><strong>📈 Zoom in: </strong>Demand for facial massage has grown at Snead's <a href=\"https://link.axios.com/click/47993161.432298/aHR0cHM6Ly93d3cuYmVya2FuYS5zdHVkaW8vYWJvdXQ_dXRtX3NvdXJjZT1uZXdzbGV0dGVyJnV0bV9tZWRpdW09ZW1haWwmdXRtX2NhbXBhaWduPW5ld3NsZXR0ZXJfYXhpb3NmaW5pc2hsaW5lJnN0cmVhbT10b3A/6a14a774a4e0095e0a03c94aB038dbe1f\" target=\"_blank\">Berkana studio</a> in St. Louis Park, Minnesota.</p><ul><li><strong>Four</strong> <strong>years ago,</strong> she performed roughly two or three a week. Now, she may do as many as 20, she says.</li><li><strong>FaceGym,</strong> a facial massage chain founded in London, has <a href=\"https://link.axios.com/click/47993161.432298/aHR0cHM6Ly91c2EuZmFjZWd5bS5jb20vcGFnZXMvZmluZC1hLXN0dWRpbz91dG1fc291cmNlPW5ld3NsZXR0ZXImdXRtX21lZGl1bT1lbWFpbCZ1dG1fY2FtcGFpZ249bmV3c2xldHRlcl9heGlvc2ZpbmlzaGxpbmUmc3RyZWFtPXRvcA/6a14a774a4e0095e0a03c94aB8d88d08c\" target=\"_blank\">two more U.S. locations planned</a>, adding to its seven already open in New York and Los Angeles.</li></ul><p>😮‍💨 <strong>How it works:</strong> Facial massage takes many forms, including <a href=\"https://link.axios.com/click/47993161.432298/aHR0cHM6Ly9oZWFsdGguY2xldmVsYW5kY2xpbmljLm9yZy93aHktZ3VhLXNoYS1taWdodC1iZS1nb29kLWZvci15b3U_dXRtX3NvdXJjZT1uZXdzbGV0dGVyJnV0bV9tZWRpdW09ZW1haWwmdXRtX2NhbXBhaWduPW5ld3NsZXR0ZXJfYXhpb3NmaW5pc2hsaW5lJnN0cmVhbT10b3A/6a14a774a4e0095e0a03c94aBc1225d90\" target=\"_blank\">gua sha</a>, a technique rooted in centuries-old Chinese medicine that uses a smooth-edged tool to massage or scrape the skin.</p><ul><li><strong>Snead starts</strong> with warm gua sha stones, then uses her hands to massage facial muscles before finishing with cool stones.</li><li><strong>Clients often say</strong> their faces feel \"lighter\" and less puffy afterward. Some even cry, which Snead describes as an emotional release.</li></ul><p><strong>What they're saying:</strong> Facial massage \"would conceivably have the same physiological effects as massaging other parts of the body,\" says Tiffany Field, a faculty member at the University of Miami School of Medicine who studies massage.</p><p>💤 <strong>Reality check:</strong> Research on facial massage is limited, though small studies suggest it may help people <a href=\"https://link.axios.com/click/47993161.432298/aHR0cHM6Ly9wdWJtZWQubmNiaS5ubG0ubmloLmdvdi8zODU2MTY0My8_dXRtX3NvdXJjZT1uZXdzbGV0dGVyJnV0bV9tZWRpdW09ZW1haWwmdXRtX2NhbXBhaWduPW5ld3NsZXR0ZXJfYXhpb3NmaW5pc2hsaW5lJnN0cmVhbT10b3A/6a14a774a4e0095e0a03c94aB79e2a1dd\" target=\"_blank\">sleep better</a>. Studies of facial rollers also suggest they may <a href=\"https://link.axios.com/click/47993161.432298/aHR0cHM6Ly9wdWJtZWQubmNiaS5ubG0ubmloLmdvdi8zMDQ3Nzg1Mi8_dXRtX3NvdXJjZT1uZXdzbGV0dGVyJnV0bV9tZWRpdW09ZW1haWwmdXRtX2NhbXBhaWduPW5ld3NsZXR0ZXJfYXhpb3NmaW5pc2hsaW5lJnN0cmVhbT10b3A/6a14a774a4e0095e0a03c94aB3865f1d4\" target=\"_blank\">boost blood flow</a> and <a href=\"https://link.axios.com/click/47993161.432298/aHR0cHM6Ly9wbWMubmNiaS5ubG0ubmloLmdvdi9hcnRpY2xlcy9QTUMxMjEyMTMyNC8_dXRtX3NvdXJjZT1uZXdzbGV0dGVyJnV0bV9tZWRpdW09ZW1haWwmdXRtX2NhbXBhaWduPW5ld3NsZXR0ZXJfYXhpb3NmaW5pc2hsaW5lJnN0cmVhbT10b3A/6a14a774a4e0095e0a03c94aB262e10a7\" target=\"_blank\">improve skin elasticity</a>.</p><ul><li><strong>FaceGym </strong><a href=\"https://link.axios.com/click/47993161.432298/aHR0cHM6Ly91c2EuZmFjZWd5bS5jb20vcGFnZXMvb3VyLXN0b3J5P3V0bV9zb3VyY2U9bmV3c2xldHRlciZ1dG1fbWVkaXVtPWVtYWlsJnV0bV9jYW1wYWlnbj1uZXdzbGV0dGVyX2F4aW9zZmluaXNobGluZSZzdHJlYW09dG9w/6a14a774a4e0095e0a03c94aB7a2361b8\" target=\"_blank\"><strong>promotes</strong></a><strong> </strong>cosmetic benefits, including lifting, sculpting and toning facial muscles, but the evidence for lasting cosmetic improvements remains limited.</li></ul><p>😌 <strong>Try it yourself:</strong> Snead recommends gently rolling a jade roller from the nose toward the ear and then down the neck.</p><ul><li><strong>\"It doesn't have</strong> to be a long time,\" she says.</li></ul><p><strong>The bottom line:</strong> For many clients, the appeal is simple: \"A rest, a little breath, a little peace for a second,\" Snead says.</p><ul><li><a href=\"https://link.axios.com/click/47993161.432298/aHR0cHM6Ly93d3cuYXhpb3MuY29tL2xvY2FsL3R3aW4tY2l0aWVzLzIwMjYvMTAvMTYvZmFjaWFsLW1hc3NhZ2UtZ3VhLXNoYS1qYWRlLXJvbGxlcj91dG1fc291cmNlPW5ld3NsZXR0ZXImdXRtX21lZGl1bT1lbWFpbCZ1dG1fY2FtcGFpZ249bmV3c2xldHRlcl9heGlvc2ZpbmlzaGxpbmUmc3RyZWFtPXRvcA/6a14a774a4e0095e0a03c94aB08fb3d97\" target=\"_blank\"><em>Share this story</em></a><em>.</em></li></ul></td>\r\n</tr> <tr><td align=\"center\" style=\"padding:20px 3.5% 25px\">   <a href=\"https://link.axios.com/click/47993161.432298/aHR0cHM6Ly93d3cuZmFjZWJvb2suY29tL3NoYXJlci5waHA_dT1odHRwczovL3d3dy5heGlvcy5jb20vbmV3c2xldHRlcnMvYXhpb3MtZmluaXNoLWxpbmUtNDE0MWU0OTUtYzNkYS00YmY4LTk3YWMtZWU5MTE3NGU5YTI4Lmh0bWw_Y2h1bmslM0QxJTI2dXRtX3Rlcm0lM0RmYnNvY2lhbHNoYXJlJTIzc3RvcnkxJnV0bV9zb3VyY2U9bmV3c2xldHRlciZ1dG1fbWVkaXVtPWVtYWlsJnV0bV9jYW1wYWlnbj1uZXdzbGV0dGVyX2F4aW9zZmluaXNobGluZSZzdHJlYW09dG9w/6a14a774a4e0095e0a03c94aBe263fb38\" style=\"display:inline-block\"><img width=\"32\" height=\"32\" style=\"border:0\" src=\"https://static.axios.com/img/axios-site/newsletters/logos/footer/share-facebook-circle-border.png\" alt=\"Share on Facebook\"></a> <a href=\"https://link.axios.com/click/47993161.432298/aHR0cHM6Ly90d2l0dGVyLmNvbS9pbnRlbnQvdHdlZXQ_\" style=\"display:inline-block;margin-left:7px\"><img width=\"32\" height=\"32\" style=\"border:0\" src=\"https://static.axios.com/img/axios-site/newsletters/logos/footer/share-x-circle-border.png\" alt=\"Tweet this Story\"></a> <a href=\"https://link.axios.com/click/47993161.\" style=\"display:inline-block;margin-left:7px\"><img width=\"32\" height=\"32\" style=\"border:0\" src=\"https://static.axios.com/img/axios-site/newsletters/logos/footer/share-linkedin-circle-border.png\" alt=\"Post to LinkedIn\"></a>  <a href=\"mailto:?subject=From Axios: 1 big thing: Your face needs a break&body=teruyuki%40hh.iij4u.or.jp%20has%20shared%20an%20Axios%20story%20with%20you%3A%0A%0A1 big thing: Your face needs a break%0Ahttp